   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRC has secured a second allocation of&#xa0;&#xa3;610,240.71&#xa0;to the Zambia CATI project. The second allocation will focus on Empowering Community Structures for Preparedness and Response in additional districts.&#xa0;A total of &#xa3;601,945.11 will be transferred to IFRC, with the grant expected to support additional infrastructural components as well as building of community structures to support cholera preparedness.&#xa0;
&#xa0;
As part of complementing and strengthening sustainability of the CATI initiative, the equivalent of USD 100,000 from this grant will be used by IFRC to match the Government of Zambia&#x2019;s contribution to the Africa Risk Capacity (ARC).</narrative>
